{"t": 1098.39, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 3, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "PSSHI_FBR_LC", "rationale": "The previous design (PSSHI_FBR_Zener) failed due to a conflict between ripple and settling time: a large Cout reduced ripple but caused the output mean to drift (long RC time constant), while a small Cout improved settling but increased ripple. To decouple these, I am introducing an LC filter at the output of the rectifier. The inductor (L2) smooths the charging current pulses from the FBR, allowing for a smaller Cout that satisfies the settling time (dv) and startup (tup) constraints while maintaining low peak-to-peak ripple (vpp).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "PSSHI_FBR_LC", "rationale": "The previous design (PSSHI_FBR_Zener) failed due to a conflict between ripple and settling time: a large Cout reduced ripple but caused the output mean to drift (long RC time constant), while a small Cout improved settling but increased ripple. To decouple these, I am introducing an LC filter at the output of the rectifier. The inductor (L2) smooths the charging current pulses from the FBR, allowing for a smaller Cout that satisfies the settling time (dv) and startup (tup) constraints while maintaining low peak-to-peak ripple (vpp).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0002, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n2"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-06}, {"id": "Dz", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
